lic><bold>120</bold>, 10203&#x02013;10209.</citation></ref><ref id="bb26"><citation citation-type="other">Grzesiek, S. &#x00026; Bax, A. (1993). <italic>J. Am. Chem. Soc.</italic><bold>115</bold>, 12593&#x02013;12594.</citation></ref><ref id="bb27"><citation citation-type="other">Gu, Y., Kar, T. &#x00026; Scheiner, S. (1999). <italic>J. Am. Chem. Soc.</italic><bold>121</bold>, 9411&#x02013;9422.</citation></ref><ref id="bb28"><citation citation-type="other">Gutteridge, A. &#x00026; Thornton, J. M. (2005). <italic>Trends Biochem. Sci.</italic><bold>30</bold>, 622&#x02013;629.</citation></ref><ref id="bb29"><citation citation-type="other">Hamelryck, T. &#x00026; Manderick, B. (2003). <italic>Bioinformatics</italic>, <bold>19</bold>, 2308&#x02013;2310.</citation></ref><ref id="bb30"><citation citation-type="other">Harris, R. K., Becker, E. D., Cabral de Menezes, S. M., Goodfellow, R. &#x00026; Granger, P. (2001). <italic>Pure Appl. Chem.</italic><bold>73</bold>, 1795&#x02013;1818.</citation></ref><ref id="bb31"><citation citation-type="other">Hubbard, S. J. &#x00026; Thornton, J. M. (1993). <italic>NACCESS Computer Program.</italic> Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology, University College London.</citation></ref><ref id="bb33"><citation citation-type="other">Jeffrey, G. A. (1997). <italic>An Introduction to Hydrogen Bonding.</italic> Oxford University Press.</citation></ref><ref id="bb32"><citation citation-type="other">Jeffrey, G. A. &#x00026; Yeon, Y. (1986). <italic>Acta Cryst.</italic> B<bold>42</bold>, 410&#x02013;413.</citation></ref><ref id="bb34"><citation citation-type="other">Kauppinen, S., Christgau, S., Kofod, L. V., Halkier, T., D&#x000f6;rreich, K. &#x00026; Dalb&#x000f8;ge, H. (1995). <italic>J. Biol. Chem.</italic><bold>270</bold>, 27172&#x02013;27178.</citation></ref><ref id="bb35"><citation citation-type="other">Kissinger, C. R., Gehlhaar, D. K., Smith, B. A. &#x00026; Bouzida, D. (2001). <italic>Acta Cryst.</italic> D<bold>57</bold>, 1474&#x02013;1479.</citation></ref><ref id="bb36"><citation citation-type="other">Kleywegt, G. J. &#x00026; Jones, T. A. (1996). <italic>Structure</italic>, <bold>4</bold>, 1395&#x02013;1400.</citation></ref><ref id="bb37"><citation citation-type="other">Li, H. &#x00026; Jensen, J. H. (2004). <italic>J. Comput. Chem.</italic><bold>25</bold>, 1449&#x02013;1462.</citation></ref><ref id="bb38"><citation citation-type="other">Li, H., Robertson, A. D. &#x00026; Jensen, J. H. (2005). <italic>Proteins</italic>, <bold>61</bold>, 704&#x02013;721.</citation></ref><ref id="bb39"><citation citation-type="other">McDonald, I. K. &#x00026; Thornton, J. M. (1994). <italic>J. Mol. Biol.</italic><bold>238</bold>, 777&#x02013;793.</citation></ref><ref id="bb40"><citation citation-type="other">Madsen, D., Flensburg, C. &#x00026; Larsen, S. (1998). <italic>J. Phys. Chem. A</italic>, <bold>102</bold>, 2177&#x02013;2188.</citation></ref><ref id="bb41"><citation citation-type="other">Markley, J. L. &#x00026; Westler, W. M. (1996). <italic>Biochemistry</italic>, <bold>35</bold>, 11092&#x02013;11097.</citation></ref><ref id="bb44"><citation citation-type="other">M&#x000f8;lgaard, A. (2000). PhD thesis. University of Copenhagen, Denmark.</citation></ref><ref id="bb45"><citation citation-type="other">M&#x000f8;lgaard, A., Kauppinen, S. &#x00026; Larsen, S. (2000). <italic>Structure</italic>, <bold>8</bold>, 373&#x02013;383.</citation></ref><ref id="bb46"><citation citation-type="other">M&#x000f8;lgaard, A. &#x00026; Larsen, S. (2002). <italic>Acta Cryst.</italic> D<bold>58</bold>, 111&#x02013;119.</citation></ref><ref id="bb47"><citation citation-type="other">M&#x000f8;lgaard, A. &#x00026; Larsen, S. (2004). <italic>Acta Cryst.</italic> D<bold>60</bold>, 472&#x02013;478.</citation></ref><ref id="bb48"><citation citation-type="other">M&#x000f8;lgaard, A., Petersen, J. F. W., Kauppinen, S., Dalb&#x000f8;ge, H., Johnsen, A. H., Navarro Poulsen, J.-C. &#x00026; Larsen, S. (1998). <italic>Acta Cryst.</italic> D<bold>54</bold>, 1026&#x02013;1029.</citation></ref><ref id="bb42"><citation citation-type="other">Molina, P. A. &#x00026; Jensen, J. H. (2003). <italic>J. Phys. Chem. B</italic>, <bold>107</bold>, 6226&#x02013;6233.</citation></ref><ref id="bb43"><citation citation-type="other">Murzin, A. G., Brenner, S. E., Hubbard, T. &#x00026; Chothia, C. (1995). <italic>J. Mol. Biol.</italic><bold>247</bold>, 536&#x02013;540.</citation></ref><ref id="bb49"><citation citation-type="other">Olovsson, I. &#x00026; J&#x000f6;nsson, P.-G. (1976). <italic>The Hydrogen Bond</italic>, Vol. II, edited by P. Schuster, G. Zundel &#x00026; C. Sandorfy, pp. 395&#x02013;456. Amsterdam: North-Holland Publishing Co.</citation></ref><ref id="bb50"><citation citation-type="other">Otwinowski, Z. &#x00026; Minor, W. (1997). <italic>Methods Enzymol.</italic><bold>276</bold>, 307&#x02013;326.</citation></ref><ref id="bb51"><citation citation-type="other">Piana, S. &#x00026; Carloni, P. (2000). <italic>Proteins</italic>, <bold>39</bold>, 26&#x02013;36.</citation></ref><ref id="bb52"><citation citation-type="other">Porter, C. T., Bartlett, G. J. &#x00026; Thornton, J. M. (2004). <italic>Nucleic Acids. Res.</italic><bold>32</bold>, D129&#x02013;D133.</citation></ref><ref id="bb53"><citation citation-type="other">Porter, M. A. &#x00026; Molina, P. A. (2006). <italic>J. Chem. Theory Comput.</italic><bold>2</bold>, 1675&#x02013;1684.</citation></ref><ref id="bb54"><citation citation-type="other">Porubcan, M. A., Neves, D. E., Rausch, S. K. &#x00026; Markley, J. L. (1978). <italic>Biochemistry</italic>, <bold>17</bold>, 4640&#x02013;4647.</citation></ref><ref id="bb55"><citation citation-type="other">Qin, J., Clore, M. &#x00026; Gronenborn, A. M. (1996). <italic>Biochemistry</italic>, <bold>35</bold>, 7&#x02013;13.</citation></ref><ref id="bb56"><citation citation-type="other">Rablen, P. R., Pearlman, S. A. &#x00026; Finkbiner, J. (1999). <italic>J. Phys. Chem. A</italic>, <bold>103</bold>, 7357&#x02013;7363.</citation></ref><ref id="bb57"><citation citation-type="other">Rajagopal, S. &#x00026; Vishveshwara, S. (2005). <italic>FEBS J.</italic><bold>272</bold>, 1819&#x02013;1832.</citation></ref><ref id="bb58"><citation citation-type="other">Robillard, G. &#x00026; Shulman, R. G. (1972). <italic>J. Mol. Biol.</italic><bold>71</bold>, 507&#x02013;511.</citation></ref><ref id="bb59"><citation citation-type="other">Sawyer, L. &#x00026; James, M. N. G. (1982). <italic>Nature (London)</italic>, <bold>295</bold>, 79&#x02013;80.</citation></ref><ref id="bb60"><citation citation-type="other">Seavey, B. R., Farr, E. A., Westler, W. M. &#x00026; Markley, J. L. (1991). <italic>J. Biomol. NMR</italic>, <bold>1</bold>, 217&#x02013;236.</citation></ref><ref id="bb61"><citation citation-type="other">Schmidt, M. W., Baldridge, K. K., Boatz, J. A., Elbert, S. T., Gordon, M. S., Jensen, J. H., Koseki, S., Matsunaga, N., Nguyen, K. A., Su, S. J., Windus, T. L., Dupuis, M. &#x00026; Montgomery, J. A. (1993). <italic>J. Comput. Chem.</italic><bold>14</bold>, 1347&#x02013;1363.</citation></ref><ref id="bb62"><citation citation-type="other">Schutz, C. N. &#x00026; Warshel, A. (2004). <italic>Proteins</italic>, <bold>55</bold>, 711&#x02013;723.</citation></ref><ref id="bb63"><citation citation-type="other">Sheldrick, G. M. (2008). <italic>Acta Cryst.</italic> A<bold>64</bold>, 112&#x02013;122.</citation></ref><ref id="bb64"><citation citation-type="other">Vaguine, A. A., Richelle, J. &#x00026; Wodak, S. J. (1999). <italic>Acta Cryst.</italic> D<bold>55</bold>, 191&#x02013;205.</citation></ref><ref id="bb65"><citation citation-type="other">Vriend, G. (1990). <italic>J. Mol. Graph.</italic><bold>8</bold>, 52&#x02013;56.</citation></ref><ref id="bb66"><citation citation-type="other">Wang, G. &#x00026; Dunbrack, R. L. Jr (2003). <italic>Bioinformatics</italic>, <bold>19</bold>, 1589&#x02013;1591.</citation></ref><ref id="bb67"><citation citation-type="other">Weber, I. T., Kovalevsky, A. Y. &#x00026; Harrison, R. W. (2007). <italic>Frontiers Drug Des. Discov.</italic><bold>3</bold>, 45&#x02013;62.</citation></ref><ref id="bb68"><citation citation-type="other">Wlodawer, A., Li, M., Gustchina, A., Dauter, Z., Uchida, K., Oyama, H., Goldfarb, N. E., Dunn, B. M. &#x00026; Oda, K. (2001). <italic>Biochemistry</italic>, <bold>40</bold>, 15602&#x02013;15611.</citation></ref><ref id="bb69"><citation citation-type="other">Wohlfahrt, G. (2005). <italic>Proteins</italic>, <bold>58</bold>, 396&#x02013;406.</citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><fig id="fig1" position="float"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Overall structure of RGAE D192N excluding Thr79 and Ser80, which could not be located in the density maps. The terminal residues Thr1 and Leu233 are labelled. The three residues corresponding to the catalytic triad (Ser9-His195-Asn192) are coloured green and the GlcNAc moieties and acetate ion are illustrated by spheres. The short hydrogen bonds in Table 4<xref ref-type="table" rid="table4"> &#x025b6;</xref> are shown as dashed lines.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="d-64-00851-fig1"/></fig><fig id="fig2" position="float"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>Stereo figure showing the active-site His195&#x02013;Asp192/His195&#x02013;Asn192 and His193&#x02013;Glu140 interactions in wild-type RGAE and RGAE D192N in lighter and darker shades, respectively.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="d-64-00851-fig2"/></fig><fig id="fig3" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Stereo figure showing the Asp75&#x02013;Asp87 area and oxyanion hole in wild-type RGAE and RGAE D192N in lighter and darker shades, respectively.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="d-64-00851-fig3"/></fig><fig id="fig4" position="float"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>                  <sup>1</sup>H NMR spectra of wild-type RGAE (<italic>a</italic>) and RGAE D192N (<italic>b</italic>) at various pH values.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="d-64-00851-fig4"/></fig><fig id="fig5" position="float"><label>Figure 5</label><caption><p>Histograms showing the distribution of distances in the Cambridge Structural Database for some of the short hydrogen-bond types present in RGAE.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="d-64-00851-fig5"/></fig><fig id="fig6" position="float"><label>Figure 6</label><caption><p>Examples of different types of short hydrogen bonds from the RGAE D192N structure. (<italic>a</italic>) Asp75&#x02013;Asp87, (<italic>b</italic>) Thr10&#x02013;Asp8, (<italic>c</italic>) Thr20&#x02013;Gly17, (<italic>d</italic>) Val3&#x02013;Thr34, (<italic>e</italic>) His169&#x02013;Glu70 and Ser131&#x02013;Glu70, (<italic>f</italic>) Arg46&#x02013;Asp82 and Ser98&#x02013;Asp82.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="d-64-00851-fig6"/></fig><table-wrap id="table1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><title>Data-collection and refinement statistics for RGAE D192N</title><p>Values in parentheses are for the outer resolution shell.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><tbody valign="top"><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1" align="left" valign="top">Total No. of reflections </td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1" align="left" valign="top">497682 </td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1" align="left" valign="top">Unique reflections </td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1" align="left" valign="top">55818 </td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1" align="left" valign="top">Resolution range (&#x000c5;) </td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1" align="left" valign="top">19.73&#x02013;1.33 (1.35&#x02013;1.33) </td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1" align="left" valign="top">Completeness (%) </td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1" align="left" valign="top">99.5 (98.3) </td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1" align="left" valign="top"><italic>I</italic>/&#x003c3;(<italic>I</italic>)&#x000a0;&#x0003e; 2 (%) </td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1" align="left" valign="top">91.3 (72.8) </td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1" align="left" valign="top"><italic>R</italic><sub>merge